      </property>
      <layout class="QVBoxLayout" name="verticalLayout_2">
       <item>
        <widget class="QLabel" name="lblHelptext">
         <property name="text">
          <string>&lt;html&gt;&lt;head/&gt;&lt;body&gt;&lt;p&gt;Every Windows has a desktop calculator with many features but &lt;span style=&quot; font-weight:600;&quot;&gt;FalconCalc&lt;/span&gt; offers many unique features not found in them.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-weight:600;&quot;&gt;FalconCalc&lt;/span&gt; continuously evaluates expressions as they are entered. Those may contain &lt;span style=&quot; font-style:italic;&quot;&gt;built-in&lt;/span&gt; and &lt;span style=&quot; font-style:italic;&quot;&gt;user defined&lt;/span&gt; constants&lt;br/&gt;and functions of any number of arguments with many important digits &lt;br/&gt;(currently maximum # of digits is 65, but can be set any number, if you compile your own exe).&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;Results are displayed simultaneously as &lt;span style=&quot; font-style:italic;&quot;&gt;decimal&lt;/span&gt;, &lt;span style=&quot; font-style:italic;&quot;&gt;hexadecimal&lt;/span&gt;, &lt;span style=&quot; font-style:italic;&quot;&gt;octal&lt;/span&gt; and &lt;span style=&quot; font-style:italic;&quot;&gt;binary&lt;/span&gt; numbers and as a string of characters.&lt;br/&gt;The display format of the numbers is selectable as simple text, as &lt;span style=&quot; font-style:italic;&quot;&gt;HTML&lt;/span&gt; encoded text, or a TEX format text.&lt;br/&gt;By clicking on the corresponding button the result can be copied to the clipboard in any of these formats.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;You may enter arithmetic formulas, use logical operations, pre-defined constants and functions and can define&lt;br/&gt;your own constants and functions as well. &lt;span style=&quot; font-weight:600;&quot;&gt;FalconCalc&lt;/span&gt; remebers your previous formulas too.&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-weight:600;&quot;&gt;Arithmetic formulas&lt;/span&gt; may contain the following operators:&lt;br/&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-style:italic;&quot;&gt;+, -, *, /, ^&lt;/span&gt; (power), &lt;span style=&quot; font-style:italic;&quot;&gt;|&lt;/span&gt; (or &lt;span style=&quot; font-style:italic;&quot;&gt;'or'&lt;/span&gt;), &amp;amp; (or &lt;span style=&quot; font-style:italic;&quot;&gt;'and'&lt;/span&gt;), &lt;span style=&quot; font-style:italic;&quot;&gt;xor&lt;/span&gt;, &lt;span style=&quot; font-style:italic;&quot;&gt;(or 'shl' -shift left), (or 'shr' -shift right),&lt;br/&gt;% (or mod) - &lt;/span&gt;remainder&lt;span style=&quot; font-style:italic;&quot;&gt;, '~' - bit negation, ¬ - logical negation&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-style:italic;&quot;&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-weight:600; font-style:italic;&quot;&gt;Logical operators&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-style:italic;&quot;&gt;:&lt;br/&gt;==, != (not equal), , = (these results in 1 or 0), ! (factorial)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-weight:600; font-style:italic;&quot;&gt;Built-in functions&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-style:italic;&quot;&gt; (alternative names in parenthesis):&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;abs, arcsin(asin), arccos(acos), arctan(atan), cos, cosh(ch), coth(cth), exp, fact, frac, int,&lt;br/&gt;log(ln), log2, log10(lg), round, sign, sin, sinh(sh), sqrt, tan(tg), trunc&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-weight:600; font-style:italic;&quot;&gt;Built in mathematical constants&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-style:italic;&quot;&gt;:&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-weight:600;&quot;&gt;e&lt;/span&gt; (base of the natural logarithm),&lt;br/&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-weight:600;&quot;&gt;log2e&lt;/span&gt; (base 2 logarithm of e),&lt;br/&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-weight:600;&quot;&gt;log10e&lt;/span&gt; (or &lt;span style=&quot; font-weight:600;&quot;&gt;lge&lt;/span&gt; - base 10 logarithm of e),&lt;br/&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-weight:600;&quot;&gt;ln2&lt;/span&gt; (natural logarithm of 2)&lt;br/&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-weight:600;&quot;&gt;pi&lt;/span&gt;(or &lt;span style=&quot; font-weight:600;&quot;&gt;π&lt;/span&gt;), &lt;br/&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-weight:600;&quot;&gt;pi2&lt;/span&gt; (π/2),&lt;br/&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-weight:600;&quot;&gt;pi4&lt;/span&gt; (π/4),&lt;br/&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-weight:600;&quot;&gt;ppi&lt;/span&gt; (1/π),&lt;br/&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-weight:600;&quot;&gt;tpi&lt;/span&gt; (2/√π),&lt;br/&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-weight:600;&quot;&gt;sqpi&lt;/span&gt; (√π),&lt;br/&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-weight:600;&quot;&gt;sqrt2&lt;/span&gt; (√2),&lt;br/&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-weight:600;&quot;&gt;psqrt2&lt;/span&gt; (1/√2),&lt;br/&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-weight:600;&quot;&gt;sqrt3&lt;/span&gt; (√3), sqrt3P2 (√3/2)&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-weight:600;&quot;&gt;Built-in physical constants&lt;/span&gt;:&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-weight:600;&quot;&gt;au&lt;/span&gt; - astronomical unit [m],&lt;br/&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-weight:600;&quot;&gt;c&lt;/span&gt; - speed of light in vacuum (definition - exact value) [m/s], &lt;br/&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-weight:600;&quot;&gt;h&lt;/span&gt; - Planck constant [Js],&lt;br/&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-weight:600;&quot;&gt;hbar&lt;/span&gt; - reduced Planck constant [Js],&lt;br/&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-weight:600;&quot;&gt;qe&lt;/span&gt; - elementary charge [As],&lt;br/&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-weight:600;&quot;&gt;me&lt;/span&gt; - electron mass [kg],&lt;br/&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-weight:600;&quot;&gt;mp&lt;/span&gt; - proton mass [kg], &lt;br/&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-weight:600; text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;u&lt;/span&gt; - atomic mass unit [1],&lt;br/&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-weight:600;&quot;&gt;k&lt;/span&gt; - Boltzmann constant [J/K],&lt;br/&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-weight:600;&quot;&gt;G&lt;/span&gt; - Newtonian constant of gravitation [m^3/kg/s^2],&lt;br/&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-weight:600;&quot;&gt;ge&lt;/span&gt; - mean value of the gravitational acceleration on Earth (9.81 m/s²)&lt;br/&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-weight:600;&quot;&gt;eps0&lt;/span&gt;- electric constant (vacuum permittivity) exact value [F /m]&lt;br/&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-weight:600;&quot;&gt;mu0&lt;/span&gt; - magnetic constant (vacuum permeability) exact value [N/A²] = 4π·10&lt;span style=&quot; vertical-align:super;&quot;&gt;-7&lt;/span&gt;, &lt;span style=&quot; font-weight:600;&quot;&gt;&lt;br/&gt;kc&lt;/span&gt; - Coulomb's constant 1/4π eps0 [N m^2/C²],&lt;br/&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-weight:600;&quot;&gt;LA&lt;/span&gt; - Avogadro's number [1/mol],&lt;br/&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-weight:600;&quot;&gt;re&lt;/span&gt; - Earth's radius [m],&lt;br/&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-weight:600;&quot;&gt;rg&lt;/span&gt; - molar gas constant (8.31 J/ mol K),&lt;br/&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-weight:600;&quot;&gt;rs&lt;/span&gt; - Sun's radius [m]&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;Any number of user constants and functions may be defined with any valid arithmetic formula including other constants and variables:&lt;br/&gt;Line format: name = expression&lt;span style=&quot; font-weight:600;&quot;&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;comment&lt;span style=&quot; font-weight:600;&quot;&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;unit, where name may be a variable name or a function name like '&lt;span style=&quot; font-style:italic;&quot;&gt;a(x,y)&lt;/span&gt;'&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-weight:600;&quot;&gt;Examples&lt;/span&gt;:&lt;br/&gt;constR = 8.31446261815324:Universal gas constant:J/K/mol&lt;br/&gt;quad(a, b, c, s) = (-b + s * sqrt(b ^ 2 - 4 * a * c)) / 2 / a:solves the quadratic equation ax² + bx + c = 0&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;When a variable is modified the value of all dependent variables and functions are automatically changed&lt;br/&gt;Functions may have any number of arguments with any names that is different from the name of any built-in function or constant.&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/body&gt;&lt;/html&gt;</string>
         </property>
         <property name="alignment">
          <set>Qt::AlignJustify|Qt::AlignTop</set>
         </property>
         <property name="wordWrap">
          <bool>true</bool>
         </property>
        </widget>
       </item>
      </layout>
     </widget>
    </widget>
   </item>
